local E = ns.DB.entries
E["npc:bruegal-ironknuckle"] = {t="npc",n="Bruegal Ironknuckle",z="stockade",s="Bruegal Ironknuckle is an infamous dwarven prisoner held within the Stormwind Stockade. Unlike the petty criminals and rioting rabble that fill the holding cells, he is a formidable brawler whose presence deep inside the corridors spells immediate danger to anyone trying to restore order.",h="Bruegal Ironknuckle is an infamous dwarven prisoner held within the Stormwind Stockade.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Convict",b="When the Stormwind Stockade erupted into open revolt, many of the city's most volatile cutthroats took control of the subterranean cellblocks. Among them is Bruegal Ironknuckle, a particularly dangerous dwarf inmate known for brutal brawling strength. Rather than staying confined to a single cell, he prowls the riot-torn hallways, ready to bash anyone attempting to quell the uprising.",sp=0},{t="Unruly Outlaw",b="While much of the uprising inside the facility is orchestrated by the Defias Brotherhood and their ringleaders, inmates like Bruegal highlight that the prison houses assorted rogues and outlaws from across the eastern realms. Whatever crimes earned him a sentence deep beneath Stormwind, his fierce resilience makes him an elusive target and one of the deadliest lone inmates walking the prison corridors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bruegal Ironknuckle?",a="Bruegal Ironknuckle is an elite dwarven convict imprisoned in the Stormwind Stockade. He is known as an elusive, tough inmate who wanders the prison halls during the ongoing riot.",al={"who is bruegal","ironknuckle lore","stockade dwarf prisoner"}},{q="Is Bruegal Ironknuckle part of the Defias Brotherhood?",a="He is not a sworn member of the Defias Brotherhood, though he benefits from their uprising. The Stockade holds a wide assortment of criminals, thieves, and violent malcontents, and Bruegal is among the independent cutthroats taking full advantage of the chaos.",al={"is bruegal defias","defias dwarf stockade"}},{q="Why is he imprisoned in the Stockade?",a="The exact charges that landed him in the Stockade are not recorded in official public warrants, but his violent temper and brawling reputation suggest serious offenses against the laws of Stormwind.",al={"why is bruegal locked up","bruegal crime"}},{q="Where can he be found inside the Stockade?",a="Bruegal does not sit still in a designated cell. He is an elusive inmate who occasionally roams the inner passages and junctions of the prison, surprising those clearing out the rioters.",al={"bruegal spawn","where is bruegal","stockade rare spawn"}},{q="Is he always present in the prison?",a="No. Bruegal is a rare sight among the rioting population. He is often kept locked down or holed up out of sight, appearing only sporadically during the ongoing unrest.",al={"can bruegal not spawn","why cant i find bruegal"}},{q="What makes him notable among the prisoners?",a="Aside from his fearsome combat prowess, Bruegal is reputed to carry valuable contraband and gear hidden away from the prison guards, making him a sought-after prize for adventurers brave enough to confront him.",al={"why do people look for bruegal","bruegal significance"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven visitors may find it sobering to see a stout kinsman cast among the cutpurses and rogues of Stormwind, showing that exile and outlawry reach even Ironforge's sons.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's city guard relies on brave Alliance champions to suppress rogue elements like Ironknuckle, who threaten to turn the heart of the capital into a permanent fortress of anarchy.",["class:Warrior"]="Ironknuckle fights with raw grit and heavy fists, offering martial fighters a glimpse of what unbridled brute strength looks like when stripped of discipline and honor."},kw={"brawler","bruegal ironknuckle","dwarf","inmate","ironknuckle","prisoner","rare","stockade","stormwind"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:dwarf"},src={"Bruegal Ironknuckle"}}
E["npc:councilman-millstipe"] = {t="npc",n="Councilman Millstipe",z="stockade",s="Councilman Millstipe is a member of Darkshire's governing council, residing within the town hall of Duskwood. Deeply resentful of royal neglect and judicial meddling from the capital, he actively seeks retribution against criminals who endanger the darkened region.",h="Councilman Millstipe is a member of Darkshire's governing council, residing within the town hall of Duskwood.",sec={{t="Justice Denied by Stormwind",b="While Darkshire struggles under the shadow of the undead and ferocious beast attacks, its local council fights an uphill battle against the bureaucracy of Stormwind City. Councilman Millstipe represents the town's growing bitterness toward the crown. When the notorious grave robber Dextren Ward was caught selling freshly dug corpses to the necromancer Morbent Fel, Darkshire's leaders sentenced him to death. Instead, Stormwind's House of Nobles intervened, commuting Ward's execution and locking him safely away inside the Stormwind Stockade.",sp=0},{t="A Message to the Nobles",b="Refusing to let the capital's corrupt politicians override the safety and justice of Duskwood, Millstipe discreetly tasks adventurers with finishing the job. By ordering the summary execution of Dextren Ward within his Stockade cell, Millstipe aims to send an unmistakable message to the House of Nobles: if Stormwind refuses to protect the people of Duskwood, the people will take justice into their own hands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Councilman Millstipe be found?",a="Councilman Millstipe is located inside Darkshire's town hall, situated in the eastern part of Duskwood.",al={"millstipe location","where is millstipe","find councilman millstipe"}},{q="Why does Millstipe want Dextren Ward dead?",a="Dextren Ward was a grave robber who exhumed the dead of Duskwood and sold them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Darkshire sentenced him to hang, but Stormwind's House of Nobles spared his life and threw him into the Stockade instead.",al={"why kill dextren ward","millstipe dextren ward","ward crime"}},{q="What is Millstipe's grievance with Stormwind?",a="Millstipe believes Stormwind has abandoned Duskwood while meddling in its local justice. The House of Nobles overruled Darkshire's rightful death sentence for Dextren Ward, leaving the traumatized settlement feeling ignored and unprotected by the throne.",al={"why mad at stormwind","house of nobles darkshire","millstipe politics"}},{q="Does Millstipe have any known family?",a="He is believed to share lineage with Baroness Dorothea Millstipe, whose restless spirit haunts the banqueting halls of the abandoned tower of Karazhan in Deadwind Pass.",al={"millstipe relatives","dorothea millstipe","millstipe family"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Millstipe embodies the deep political rift between Stormwind's sheltered nobility and the desperate frontier settlements of Duskwood, which receive little aid yet face heavy-handed meddling from the capital.",["class:Rogue"]="For an operative willing to slip into the heavily guarded Stockade and carry out an unsanctioned political execution, Millstipe offers work that directly defies the House of Nobles."},kw={"councilman millstipe","darkshire","dextren ward","duskwood","house of nobles","millstipe","morbent fel","stockade"},rel={"quest:377","npc:dextren-ward","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","subzone:stormwind-stockade","quest:55","topic:house-of-nobles","subzone:karazhan"},src={"Councilman Millstipe"}}
E["npc:dextren-ward"] = {t="npc",n="Dextren Ward",z="stockade",s="Dextren Ward is an infamous criminal and grave robber locked away inside the Stormwind Stockade. Before his capture, he profited by exhuming bodies from Duskwood's Raven Hill Cemetery and delivering them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Now caught in the midst of the prison's bloody uprising, he remains marked for death by the town council of Darkshire.",h="Dextren Ward is an infamous criminal and grave robber locked away inside the Stormwind Stockade.",sec={{t="Grave Robbery in Duskwood",b="Before ending up in chains beneath the streets of Stormwind, Dextren Ward conducted a grim and lucrative business in the fog-choked woods of Duskwood. Raven Hill Cemetery was already a site of sorrow and growing horror, but Ward treated its burial grounds as a private quarry. Rather than hunting merely for trinkets and heirlooms left with the dead, Ward dealt in flesh, unearthing fresh graves to supply local dark practitioners.",sp=0},{t="Pawn of the Necromancer",b="Ward's primary customer was Morbent Fel, a necromancer whose dark rituals have plagued Duskwood and swelled the ranks of the undead. In supplying bodies to Fel, Ward actively contributed to the terror that grips Darkshire. Though eventually caught by Stormwind authorities and dragged into the Stockade, his crimes earned him the undying enmity of the people of Duskwood, prompting Councilman Millstipe to demand Ward's hand as proof of justice served.",sp=0},{t="Chaos in the Stockade",b="When a sweeping rebellion broke out inside the Stockade, Ward was not liberated by allies, but rather freed from his cell to join the chaos within the locked-down dungeon. Armed and vicious, he commands his own corner of the prison and uses terror to ward off interlopers, making him one of the priority targets Alliance forces seek to eliminate while restoring order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dextren Ward?",a="Dextren Ward is a notorious criminal imprisoned in the Stormwind Stockade. He is an elite human inmate responsible for robbing the dead in Duskwood to fuel dark rituals.",al={"who is dextren ward","dextren ward lore","stockade dextren"}},{q="Why is Dextren Ward in the Stockade?",a="Ward was captured and imprisoned for grave robbing in Duskwood's Raven Hill Cemetery. Instead of stealing valuables, he exhumed fresh corpses to sell directly to the necromancer Morbent Fel.",al={"why was he arrested","dextren ward crime","what did dextren do"}},{q="Who wants Dextren Ward dead?",a="Councilman Millstipe of Darkshire wants Ward dead. Millstipe seeks retribution for the desecration of Duskwood's graves and demands Ward's severed hand as proof of his demise.",al={"who wants dextren dead","dextren ward bounty","crime and punishment questgiver"}},{q="What is Ward's connection to Morbent Fel?",a="Ward acted as a corpse supplier for Morbent Fel. By unearthing the freshly buried dead of Raven Hill Cemetery, Ward provided the raw material Fel needed for his necromantic experiments and undead creations.",al={"morbent fel connection","dextren ward morbent fel","who bought the bodies"}},{q="Where can Dextren Ward be found?",a="He is located inside the Stormwind Stockade, the high-security prison situated in the canals of Stormwind City. He lurks in one of the holding wings during the ongoing prison revolt.",al={"dextren ward location","where is dextren ward","where to find dextren"}},{q="Why does the quest require Dextren's hand?",a="Councilman Millstipe explicitly asks for Ward's cold, dead hand as irrefutable physical proof that the grave robber can no longer dig up the graves of Duskwood or profit from necromancy.",al={"why sever his hand","dextren ward hand","proof of death dextren"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions assisting Darkshire, putting an end to Dextren Ward is an act of justice for the desecrated families of Duskwood and an essential task in reclaiming the rioting Stockade.",["class:Paladin"]="Ward's collaboration with necromancers to provide fresh corpses represents an abhorrent offense against the Sanctity of the Light and the peaceful rest of the departed.",["class:Priest"]="The desecration of holy burial ground at Raven Hill makes Ward's fate an imperative of moral and spiritual restitution."},kw={"councilman millstipe","crime and punishment","dextren ward","duskwood","grave robber","morbent fel","raven hill cemetery","stormwind","the stockade"},rel={"quest:377","zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","npc:councilman-millstipe","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","quest:55","quest:163","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Dextren Ward"}}
E["npc:guard-berton"] = {t="npc",n="Guard Berton",z="stockade",s="Guard Berton is a human town guardsman stationed outside the Lakeshire Inn in Redridge Mountains. Frustrated by the bureaucratic delays of Stormwind's legal system, he seeks swift justice against Targorr the Dread, an imprisoned orc leader.",h="Guard Berton is a human town guardsman stationed outside the Lakeshire Inn in Redridge Mountains.",sec={{t="A Guard Seeking Justice",b="While Redridge Mountains buckles under the threat of the Blackrock orc invasion, Guard Berton remains posted outside the Lakeshire Inn. Despite local defenses being pushed to the brink, Berton's attention is fixed on a captive enemy: Targorr the Dread. Targorr was captured and locked away deep within the Stormwind Stockade, sentenced to death for his crimes against the kingdom. Yet with Stormwind's execution postponed indefinitely, Berton refuses to let the brutal raider linger in a cell while Lakeshire bleeds. Taking matters into his own hands, he hires willing adventurers to bypass royal delays and execute the orc directly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Guard Berton?",a="Guard Berton is an Alliance guard stationed outside the Lakeshire Inn in the Redridge Mountains. He is primarily known for hiring adventurers to carry out justice against an infamous orc prisoner.",al={"berton lakeshire","who is berton"}},{q="Why does Guard Berton want Targorr the Dread killed?",a="Targorr the Dread was sentenced to execution for his crimes, but Stormwind's leadership placed the sentence on hold. Frustrated by this stalling while Redridge remains under siege, Berton arranges for Targorr to be eliminated inside the Stockade.",al={"why kill targorr","targorr execution","what comes around quest lore"}},{q="Where is Targorr the Dread held?",a="Targorr is confined inside the Stockade, the high-security dungeon located within the Canal district of Stormwind City.",al={"targorr location","where is targorr"}},{q="Where can Guard Berton be found?",a="He stands watch just outside the entrance to the Lakeshire Inn, overlooking the town center of Lakeshire in Redridge.",al={"where is berton","berton location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Berton represents the growing frustration among rural Alliance settlements, where local defenders watch Stormwind's central bureaucracy delay justice while border towns fight for survival."},kw={"berton","guard berton","lakeshire","redridge","targorr","targorr the dread","the stockade","what comes around"},rel={"npc:targorr-the-dread","quest:386","subzone:lakeshire-inn","subzone:lakeshire","zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Guard Berton"}}
E["npc:hamhock"] = {t="npc",n="Hamhock",z="stockade",s="Hamhock is a massive two-headed ogre confined within the depths of the Stormwind Stockade. Locked away beneath the capital alongside hardened Defias insurgents and cutthroats, he looms as a particularly brutal and unexpected inmate amidst the prison riot.",h="Hamhock is a massive two-headed ogre confined within the depths of the Stormwind Stockade.",sec={{t="A Brute Behind Bars",b="The Stormwind Stockade was built to hold petty thieves, murderers, and political dissidents, making a towering two-headed ogre an imposing sight among the cells. When the prisoners rose up and took control of the facility, Hamhock remained entrenched in the chaos, crushing anyone foolish enough to intrude on his cellblock.",sp=0},{t="Murky Origins",b="Stormwind authorities keep few public records regarding how Hamhock was captured. Popular speculation among guards and city residents suggests he may have been dragged north from the Splinter Fist clan at Duskwood's Vul'Gol Ogre Mound. Others suspect he was recruited into the Defias Brotherhood as mercenary muscle before falling into the custody of the city watch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hamhock?",a="Hamhock is an elite two-headed ogre prisoner held within the Stormwind Stockade. Amid the uprising led by the Defias convicts, he acts as a dangerous obstacle deep inside the prison corridors.",al={"hamhock","who is the ogre in stockade","ogre boss stockade"}},{q="How did an ogre end up in the Stormwind Stockade?",a="Official records do not detail his capture, but he is widely thought to either be a captured brute from the Splinter Fist clan inhabiting Duskwood or a hired enforcer employed by the Defias Brotherhood who was caught during illicit operations.",al={"why is hamhock in jail","how did hamhock get captured","why is there an ogre in stockades"}},{q="Is Hamhock allied with the Defias rioters?",a="While the entire facility has fallen into rebellion under Defias ringleaders, it is unclear whether Hamhock truly coordinates with them or simply revels in the unbridled mayhem of the broken cells.",al={"is hamhock defias","hamhock defias brotherhood","does hamhock work for bazil"}},{q="Is Hamhock related to the ogres in Duskwood?",a="Many believe he originated from the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound in Duskwood, which would place him among the Splinter Fist clan led by Zzarc'Vul prior to being captured and brought to Stormwind.",al={"is hamhock splinter fist","hamhock vulgol","vul'gol ogres stockade"}},{q="Is Hamhock tied to any specific bounty or quest?",a="No official bounties or city warrants are offered specifically for Hamhock's head. He is an incidental menace whom adventurers encounter while clearing out the rioting stronghold.",al={"hamhock quest","is there a quest for hamhock","hamhock bounty"}},{q="Why are two-headed ogres significant?",a="Two-headed ogres possess distinct personalities between their heads and are often more cunning or magically adept than their single-headed kin, making Hamhock exceptionally dangerous to standard prison guards.",al={"two headed ogre lore","why two heads"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Finding a two-headed ogre unrestrained directly beneath the capital's streets underscores just how catastrophically the city guards have lost control of the Stockade.",["class:Warrior"]="Subduing Hamhock requires meeting raw, hulking strength head-on within the tight confines of the prison hallways."},kw={"duskwood","hamhock","ogre","prison","splinter fist","stockade","stormwind","two-headed"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:vul-gol-ogre-mound","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Hamhock"}}
E["npc:kam-deepfury"] = {t="npc",n="Kam Deepfury",z="stockade",s="Kam Deepfury is a notorious Dark Iron saboteur incarcerated within the depths of the Stormwind Stockade. Unlike the majority of the prison's inmates, he has no allegiance to the Defias Brotherhood, having been captured for orchestrating a devastating explosion along the Thandol Span far to the north.",h="Kam Deepfury is a notorious Dark Iron saboteur incarcerated within the depths of the Stormwind Stockade.",sec={{t="A Saboteur Far from Home",b="While the Stockade is overwhelmingly filled with disgruntled Stonemasons and Defias rebels, Kam Deepfury stands apart. A Dark Iron dwarf of cunning and violence, Deepfury was captured and brought to Stormwind after masterminding an operation that crippled vital northern infrastructure. He is locked deep within the prison's cells, isolated from his kin beneath Blackrock Mountain but just as hostile to the Alliance as any rebel rioter sharing the corridors.",sp=0},{t="The Thandol Span Sabotage",b="Alliance intelligence stationed at Dun Modr, near the northern border of the Wetlands, identified Deepfury as the chief architect behind the explosion that shattered the Thandol Span. The blast severed one of the massive stone bridges linking the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands. Beyond crippling a critical trade and military route for Ironforge and the Alliance, the sabotage claimed the life of a kin of the dwarf commander Longbraid the Grim.",sp=0},{t="A Score to Settle",b="The Dark Iron insurrectionist did not manage to escape retribution for long, though imprisonment in Stormwind offered him temporary protection from his victims' relatives. Back in the Wetlands, Motley Garmason and the grieving Longbraid the Grim have sought mercenaries willing to infiltrate the riot-torn prison and sever Deepfury's head, settling a bloody grudge sparked hundreds of miles to the north.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kam Deepfury?",a="Kam Deepfury is an elite Dark Iron dwarf prisoner locked inside the Stormwind Stockade. He is known for orchestrating the sabotage of the Thandol Span in the north and has no ties to the Defias rebels imprisoned alongside him.",al={"who is deepfury","kam deepfury lore","who is the dwarf in stockades"}},{q="Why is a Dark Iron dwarf locked in the Stormwind Stockade?",a="Deepfury was captured after coordinating an attack that blew up one of the bridges at the Thandol Span, killing dwarven defenders and cutting off a vital land crossing between the Wetlands and Arathi. He was sent to Stormwind's high-security prison to await justice.",al={"why is he in stockade","what did kam deepfury do","why is he imprisoned"}},{q="Is Kam Deepfury part of the Defias Brotherhood?",a="No. Although he is imprisoned alongside the Defias Brotherhood during their uprising inside the Stockade, Deepfury belongs to the hostile Dark Iron clan. He acts entirely on his own clan's aggressive agenda against the Alliance and Ironforge.",al={"is he defias","kam deepfury defias","is deepfury working with vancleef"}},{q="Who wants Kam Deepfury dead?",a="Motley Garmason and the Ironforge dwarven forces stationed at Dun Modr want him dead. Longbraid the Grim lost a relative in Deepfury's bombing of the Thandol Span, prompting them to send word to adventurers in Stormwind to claim his head.",al={"who gave the quest for deepfury","who wants deepfury killed"}},{q="Where did Kam Deepfury commit his crime?",a="Deepfury organized the sabotage at the Thandol Span, the colossal bridge complex connecting the Wetlands with the Arathi Highlands far north of Stormwind.",al={"where was the bridge blown up","deepfury bridge bombing","thandol span attack"}},{q="Where can Kam Deepfury be found inside the Stockade?",a="Kam Deepfury is held within the cell blocks of the Stormwind Stockade, situated beneath the canal district of Stormwind City.",al={"where is deepfury in stockade","kam deepfury location"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, Kam Deepfury is a bitter enemy whose sabotage severed the Thandol Span and murdered the kin of Longbraid the Grim. Avenging that loss is a point of personal honor.",["faction:Alliance"]="While most eyes in Stormwind are focused on the Defias uprising, Deepfury is a reminder of the broader Dark Iron menace threatening the northern frontiers of the Alliance."},kw={"dark iron","deepfury","dun modr","garmason","kam deepfury","longbraid","stockade","stormwind","thandol span"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:dun-modr","quest:378","npc:longbraid-the-grim","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:alliance"},src={"Kam Deepfury"}}
E["npc:nikova-raskol"] = {t="npc",n="Nikova Raskol",z="stockade",s="Nikova Raskol is an elderly human townsperson who walks the cobblestone streets of Old Town in Stormwind City. Grieving the murder of her grandson at the hands of the Defias Brotherhood, she seeks justice against the rioting criminals locked inside the Stockade.",h="Nikova Raskol is an elderly human townsperson who walks the cobblestone streets of Old Town in Stormwind City.",sec={{t="A Grandmother's Grief",b="Nikova wanders Old Town carrying the weight of a recent and devastating personal tragedy. Her beloved grandson, Mac, was slain by brigands belonging to the Defias Brotherhood. While the kingdom grapples with treason on a political scale, Nikova represents the intimate human cost inflicted upon everyday citizens by the Brotherhood's lawless rampage.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance in the Stockade",b="Though many of the criminals who wrecked havoc were captured and thrown into the Stockade, prison bars offer little solace now that a violent inmate rebellion has seized the facility. Frustrated by the guards' inability to restore order, Nikova appeals directly to brave adventurers heading into the prison, asking them to collect red Defias bandanas as proof that her grandson's killers have finally faced retribution.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nikova Raskol?",a="Nikova Raskol is an elderly resident of Stormwind who walks the oval road in Old Town. She is mourning her grandson, Mac, who was murdered by Defias thugs.",al={"who is nikova","nikova raskol role","nikova raskol lore"}},{q="What happened to her grandson Mac?",a="Mac was slain in cold blood by members of the Defias Brotherhood. Many of the perpetrators ended up incarcerated in the Stormwind Stockade, where they later revolted.",al={"who is mac","what happened to mac","how did mac die"}},{q="Why does she want red bandanas from the Stockade?",a="The red bandana is the identifying mark worn by the Defias Brotherhood. Nikova asks fighters entering the rebellious Stockade to bring back these neckerchiefs to prove that the criminals responsible for taking innocent lives have been dealt with.",al={"color of blood","why red bandanas","defias bandanas"}},{q="Where can Nikova Raskol be found?",a="Nikova paces in a steady loop along the main thoroughfare of Old Town, not far from the Pig and Whistle Tavern and the training grounds in Stormwind City.",al={"where is nikova","nikova location","nikova raskol path"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions visiting Stormwind, helping Nikova is a reminder that defending the kingdom means protecting ordinary townsfolk whose families have been torn apart by civil unrest."},kw={"defias bandana","mac","nikova raskol","old town","stockade","stormwind","the color of blood"},rel={"quest:388","subzone:stormwind-stockade","subzone:old-town","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:stormwind","quest:65"},src={"Nikova Raskol"}}
E["npc:targorr-the-dread"] = {t="npc",n="Targorr the Dread",z="stockade",s="Targorr the Dread is an infamous Blackrock orc executioner imprisoned deep within the Stormwind Stockade. Known for his brutal tortures of captured Stormwind soldiers, his execution was indefinitely delayed by bureaucratic incompetence and corruption. When the Stockade erupted into revolt under the Defias Brotherhood, Targorr broke free and allied with the rioting convicts.",h="Targorr the Dread is an infamous Blackrock orc executioner imprisoned deep within the Stormwind Stockade.",sec={{t="The Butcher of Redridge",b="Before his capture, Targorr the Dread served as the supreme executioner for the Blackrock clan under Warlord Gath'Ilzogg. Operating out of the occupied ruins in Redridge, his cruelty stood out as exceptionally savage even by the violent standards of the Dark Horde. Stormwind guards and militiamen who fought to defend the borderlands were subjected to agonizing torment and slow death at his hands, making his name one of the most reviled in the kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Justice Denied",b="When Alliance forces finally managed to capture Targorr alive, he was brought in chains to the capital and locked inside the high-security Stockade to await execution. However, the rot within Stormwind's judicial and political bureaucracy stalled the proceedings. Paralyzed by graft, endless paperwork, and neglect, the courts failed to deliver the death sentence he had earned, leaving a bloodthirsty war criminal sitting in a cell beneath the heart of the city.",sp=0},{t="Uprising in the Cells",b="When the Defias Brotherhood staged their violent prison break, Targorr saw his opportunity. Breaking free from his cell, the ruthless orc threw his lot in with the Defias rioters, turning his cellblock into a slaughterhouse. With the prison entirely out of Warden Thelwater's control, towns like Lakeshire—still nursing the bitter wounds Targorr inflicted on their defenders—seek adventurers willing to venture into the riots and bring back the butcher's head.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Targorr the Dread?",a="Targorr the Dread is a Blackrock orc who served as the supreme executioner under Warlord Gath'Ilzogg. Notorious for torturing captured Stormwind soldiers, he was caught and imprisoned inside the Stormwind Stockade.",al={"who is targorr","targorr lore","stockade orc boss"}},{q="Why wasn't Targorr executed when he was captured?",a="Although Targorr was captured and scheduled to face justice, Stormwind's inefficient, bloated, and corrupt legal administration dragged out the process. His execution was delayed by endless bureaucratic red tape until the prison riots erupted.",al={"why wasn't he killed","why is targorr alive","stormwind corruption"}},{q="Why is an orc allied with the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Targorr does not share the Defias Brotherhood's political grievances, but during the chaos of the prison uprising, convicts of all stripes united against their jailers. He allied with the rioters simply to secure his freedom and slaughter any guards or adventurers who cross his path.",al={"why defias working with orcs","targorr defias ally","stockade orcs"}},{q="Who wants Targorr dead now?",a="Guard Berton, stationed at Lakeshire in Redridge, offers a bounty for Targorr's severed head. The people of Lakeshire suffered extensively under Targorr's cruelty and want to see the execution Stormwind's courts failed to deliver.",al={"who gives the targorr quest","guard berton targorr","targorr bounty"}},{q="Where can Targorr be found?",a="Targorr is located inside the Stormwind Stockade instance, holed up in one of the rear cellblocks alongside other rioting inmates.",al={"where is targorr","targorr location","stockade room"}},{q="What clan does Targorr belong to?",a="Targorr belongs to the Blackrock orcs, part of the rogue Dark Horde remnants operating out of the Redridge Mountains and Blackrock Spire, rather than the New Horde led by Thrall.",al={"targorr clan","is targorr horde","blackrock targorr"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind—particularly those with ties to Redridge—Targorr embodies the terrible cost of the kingdom's bureaucratic failures and the ongoing threat of the Blackrock orcs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Putting down Targorr within the rioting Stockade brings long-overdue justice to the fallen defenders of Lakeshire and helps contain the chaos beneath the capital."},kw={"berton","blackrock","dread","executioner","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","stockade","targorr"},rel={"zone:stockade","quest:386","npc:guard-berton","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:stormwind-stockade","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Targorr the Dread"}}
E["npc:warden-thelwater"] = {t="npc",n="Warden Thelwater",z="stockade",s="Warden Thelwater is the besieged overseer of the Stockade, Stormwind City's underground maximum-security prison. Caught unprepared when a violent riot erupted among the Defias prisoners, he now desperately recruits capable adventurers to quell the rebellion before word spreads to the city above.",h="Warden Thelwater is the besieged overseer of the Stockade, Stormwind City's underground maximum-security...",sec={{t="A Crisis in the Canals",b="Hidden beneath the canals of Stormwind, the Stockade holds the kingdom's most dangerous miscreants, petty thieves, and political conspirators. Warden Thelwater was charged with keeping them securely locked away, but an organized revolt took the guards completely off guard. With the prisoners overwhelming security and taking control of the cells, Thelwater found himself barricaded at the threshold, struggling to contain an armed insurrection right beneath the streets of the capital.",sp=0},{t="Containing the Truth",b="Rather than allowing panic to spill into the streets of Stormwind, Thelwater has chosen to handle the uprising with absolute discretion. The mastermind behind the breakout, Bazil Thredd, holds tremendous influence among the Defias Brotherhood locked inside. To prevent the riot from exposing wider vulnerabilities within Stormwind's governance, Thelwater relies on outside mercenaries to infiltrate the cellblocks, strike down the ringleaders, and quietly reclaim the facility.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Warden Thelwater?",a="Warden Thelwater is the human official stationed at the entrance of the Stockade in Stormwind City. He is responsible for managing the high-security prison complex.",al={"thelwater","stockade warden","who is thelwater"}},{q="What happened to the Stockade?",a="A coordinated revolt broke out among the prisoners, primarily driven by incarcerated members of the Defias Brotherhood. The inmates overpowered the guards and took over the cellblocks, leaving Thelwater and his remaining men pinned near the entrance.",al={"stockade riot","what happened in stockades","why is stockades broken"}},{q="Who is leading the prison riot?",a="Bazil Thredd is the mastermind orchestrating the revolt from deep inside the prison. He commands the Defias inmates and directed the sudden strike against the guards.",al={"stockade leader","who leads the uprising","who is bazil thredd"}},{q="Why hasn't the Stormwind City Guard intervened in force?",a="Thelwater aims to resolve the disaster quietly. Broadcasting that Stormwind's most fortified dungeon fell to its own inmates would ignite widespread panic across the city, so he enlists discreet adventurers to clean up the mess inside.",al={"why no guards","why hire adventurers","secret riot"}},{q="What kind of prisoners are kept here?",a="The facility holds petty crooks, thieves, murderers, hostile gnolls, and dangerous political insurgents, most notably high-ranking members of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"stockade prisoners","who is in stockade","types of criminals"}},{q="Where can Warden Thelwater be found?",a="He is stationed just inside the entrance corridor of the Stockade, located near the canals between the Mage Quarter and Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",al={"thelwater location","where is warden","find thelwater"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Warden Thelwater represents the fragile order within Stormwind, relying on loyal Alliance champions to squash the prison mutiny before it threatens the capital's citizens.",["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors dedicated to order and justice, Thelwater's desperate struggle to restore containment provides a direct call to bring righteous discipline to violent criminals.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues entering the Stockade for Thelwater find themselves navigating the messy fallout of Defias intrigue and underground prison politics."},kw={"bazil thredd","defias","prison","riot","stockade","stormwind","thelwater","warden thelwater"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","quest:391","quest:389","quest:387","quest:392","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Warden Thelwater"}}
E["quest:377"] = {t="quest",n="Crime and Punishment",z="stockade",s="Crime and Punishment is an Alliance bounty originating in Darkshire that demands the extrajudicial execution of a grave robber imprisoned within the Stormwind Stockade. Councilman Millstipe issues the contract after the House of Nobles overrides Duskwood's death sentence for Dextren Ward. Carrying out the hit satisfies local vengeance while delivering a sharp warning to the capital's negligent aristocracy.",h="Crime and Punishment is an Alliance bounty originating in Darkshire that demands the extrajudicial execution...",sec={{t="Justice Denied in Duskwood",b="Duskwood already suffers beneath a shroud of creeping horrors and official indifference from the capital. When Dextren Ward was caught digging up fresh corpses from the Darkshire cemetery to sell to the necromancer Morbent Fel, the town's ruling council showed no mercy. Lord Ello Ebonlocke sentenced the grave robber to beheadment. However, before the axe could fall, the House of Nobles intervened, claiming Ward as an imperial prisoner and transferring him to the high-security cells of the Stormwind Stockade.",sp=0},{t="An Insult to the Dead",b="To Councilman Millstipe and the grieving citizens of Darkshire, sparing Ward from the headsman's block was an intolerable insult. The nobles in their secure city showed complete disregard for the torment suffered by frontier families whose dead relatives were fed into Fel's dark craft. Frustrated by Stormwind's bureaucratic meddling, Millstipe recruits daring mercenaries to infiltrate the riotous Stockade, assassinate Ward in his cell, and sever his hand as proof of execution.",sp=0},{t="A Message to the Crown",b="Killing Ward is as much a political act as it is closure for the wronged. By ordering the assassination of a high-value prisoner under the crown's own lock and key, the Darkshire Council sends a defiant message back to Stormwind. If the nobility refuses to defend Duskwood or honor its local laws, the town has shown it will enforce its own brand of frontier justice right beneath the regent's nose.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Councilman Millstipe want Dextren Ward dead?",a="Ward was caught robbing the Darkshire cemetery, selling freshly buried corpses to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Lord Ebonlocke sentenced him to beheading, but Stormwind's House of Nobles snatched him away to lock him in the Stockade instead.",al={"why kill dextren ward","what did dextren ward do","millstipe motivation"}},{q="Where is Dextren Ward located?",a="He is held deep inside the Stormwind Stockade dungeon in the capital city of Stormwind, located along the far left corridor of the prison complex.",al={"dextren ward location","where is ward","how to find dextren ward"}},{q="Why didn't Stormwind just execute Dextren Ward?",a="The House of Nobles claimed jurisdiction over Ward for their own unspecified reasons, overruling Darkshire's local sentence and sparking outrage among Duskwood residents who feel abandoned by the capital.",al={"why was ward imprisoned","why stockade not execution"}},{q="Why does Millstipe demand Ward's hand?",a="Councilman Millstipe requires indisputable physical proof that the sentence was carried out in defiance of the House of Nobles, offering closure to the victimized families in Duskwood.",al={"hand of dextren ward","why hand proof"}},{q="Who is Morbent Fel?",a="Morbent Fel is a powerful necromancer haunting Duskwood, animating the dead and orchestrating dark rituals using bodies supplied by unscrupulous scum like Dextren Ward.",al={"who is fel","morbent fel lore"}},{q="What does this quest reveal about Duskwood's relationship with Stormwind?",a="It highlights deep political resentment. Duskwood feels neglected and unprotected by the throne, and the council's willingness to send assassins into the capital's prison shows how strained that loyalty has become.",al={"darkshire and stormwind politics","duskwood resentment"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The quest exposes severe friction within the Alliance heartland, pitting the struggling, neglected frontier of Darkshire against the distant, arrogant bureaucrats of the House of Nobles.",["class:Rogue"]="Millstipe's task is a brazen political assassination requiring a covert infiltration into the crown's own maximum-security penitentiary to bypass royal decree.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the southern kingdoms, this contract tests whether your loyalty lies with the distant crown in Stormwind or the desperate settlers holding the line in Duskwood."},kw={"darkshire","dextren ward","duskwood","grave robber","house of nobles","millstipe","morbent fel","stockade"},rel={"npc:dextren-ward","npc:councilman-millstipe","zone:stockade","zone:duskwood","quest:55","topic:house-of-nobles","subzone:darkshire","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Councilman Millstipe",["end"]="Councilman Millstipe",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=377},src={"Crime and Punishment (Classic)"}}
E["quest:378"] = {t="quest",n="The Fury Runs Deep",z="stockade",s="This quest represents Motley Garmason's bitter quest for vengeance against the Dark Iron dwarf Kam Deepfury. Deepfury masterminded the assault on the Thandol Span, which claimed the lives of Bronzebeard defenders, including Rhag Garmason. Dissatisfied with Stormwind's political detention of the culprit, Motley enlists an adventurer to enact dwarven justice inside the Stockade.",h="This quest represents Motley Garmason's bitter quest for vengeance against the Dark Iron dwarf Kam Deepfury.",sec={{t="A Grudge Across Continents",b="The northern reaches of the Wetlands bleed from perpetual clashes between the Bronzebeard defenders at Dun Modr and the insurgent Dark Iron dwarves. When the Thandol Span came under attack, the sabotage cost vital dwarven lives, including kin of Mount Mountain and Balgaras the Mountain. Intelligence gathered by Roggo revealed that Kam Deepfury planned the deceitful strike. Instead of facing execution on the front lines, however, Deepfury ended up secured inside the Stormwind Stockade—held as a political prisoner rather than executed for murder.",sp=0},{t="Dwarven Retribution vs. Human Law",b="Stationed at Dun Modr, Motley Garmason refuses to allow Stormwind's political calculations to shield a war criminal. To Motley, human bureaucracy has placed decorum above blood debts. Bound by duty to remain at Longbraid's side in the Wetlands, Motley tasks trusted champions to march deep beneath the human capital, brave the rioting Stockade, and claim Deepfury's severed head to settle the clan's score once and for all.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kam Deepfury?",a="Kam Deepfury is a treacherous Dark Iron dwarf who engineered the destructive attack on the Thandol Span. His planning led directly to the slaughter of Ironforge dwarves guarding the border crossing, making him a marked man among the survivors in Dun Modr.",al={"deepfury","kam deepfury lore","who is deepfury"}},{q="Why is Kam Deepfury imprisoned in Stormwind instead of Ironforge?",a="Stormwind authorities captured Deepfury and held him in the Stockade for undisclosed political reasons. While human leadership prefers using him as diplomatic or intelligence leverage, the dwarves of Dun Modr see this as infuriating bureaucracy that cheats them of immediate justice.",al={"why is deepfury in stockade","why stockade prisoner"}},{q="Why doesn't Motley Garmason hunt Deepfury down himself?",a="Motley is bound by honor and military duty to remain stationed at Dun Modr alongside Mount Longbraid, fighting off ongoing Dark Iron advances in the northern Wetlands. He cannot abandon the defensive line to journey south to Stormwind.",al={"why motley stay","why motley doesn't go"}},{q="What happened at the Thandol Span?",a="The Dark Iron clan executed a calculated assault on the Thandol Span bridge connecting the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands. The attack crippled a crucial Alliance supply artery and resulted in the deaths of several Bronzebeard defenders, including Longbraid's brother.",al={"thandol span attack","what happened thandol span"}},{q="Who uncovered Deepfury's role in the Thandol Span attack?",a="A dwarf named Roggo pieced together the intelligence linking Deepfury directly to the blueprint and execution of the Thandol Span offensive, handing Motley the proof he needed to demand retribution.",al={"who found deepfury","roggo intelligence"}},{q="Is Stormwind's leadership aware of the assassination inside their prison?",a="The kill order is an unsanctioned dwarven vendetta. Motley explicitly bypasses human legal channels, confident that King Magni's soldiers have every right to execute the saboteur while the Stockade is already engulfed in chaotic rioting.",al={"stormwind know about hit","is deepfury kill sanctioned"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Bronzebeard dwarves, striking down Deepfury is a solemn matter of settling a blood debt and honoring the clanmates who fell defending the Thandol Span.",["race:Human"]="Human adventurers must confront the shortcomings of their own kingdom's diplomacy, bypassing Stormwind's prison policies to satisfy their dwarven allies' code of justice.",["faction:Alliance"]="This mission highlights the underlying tensions between Stormwind's legal pragmatism and Ironforge's unyielding demand for direct vengeance in wartime."},kw={"dark iron war","deepfury","dun modr","longbraid","motley garmason","roggo","stockade","thandol span"},rel={"npc:kam-deepfury","subzone:stormwind-stockade","zone:stockade","subzone:dun-modr","quest:303","subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Motley Garmason",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=378},src={"The Fury Runs Deep"}}
E["quest:386"] = {t="quest",n="What Comes Around...",z="stockade",s="What Comes Around... is an Alliance quest offered by Guard Berton in Lakeshire, who is infuriated by the political delays surrounding an orcish war criminal. Players are directed into the Stormwind Stockade to execute Targorr the Dread before corrupt nobility can arrange his escape.",h="What Comes Around...",sec={{t="A Butcher Held in Limbo",b="Targorr the Dread gained infamy in the Redridge Mountains serving as supreme executioner under General Gath'Ilzogg, chieftain of the Blackrock orcs entrenched at Stonewatch Keep. Renowned for savage cruelty even among the Blackrock invaders, Targorr personally oversaw the torture and execution of numerous defenders of Redridge. Following his eventual capture, he was transferred to the capital's high-security prison, the Stormwind Stockade, and condemned to death for his atrocities against the realm.",sp=0},{t="Corruption in High Places",b="Despite Targorr's formal death sentence, his execution ground to a halt due to an intervention by an unnamed nobleman within Stormwind's House of Nobles. Guard Berton, stationed out in vulnerable Lakeshire, sees through the political maneuvering and suspects foul play or bribery intended to secure the brute's eventual release. Taking justice into his own hands, Berton recruits trusted adventurers to infiltrate the riot-torn prison and fulfill the execution order without bureaucratic interference.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Targorr the Dread?",a="Targorr the Dread is an elite Blackrock orc who served as the supreme executioner under General Gath'Ilzogg in Redridge. Infamous for torturing captured human soldiers, he was eventually caught and imprisoned in the Stormwind Stockade.",al={"targorr","who is targorr","targorr lore"}},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind executed Targorr yet?",a="Although sentenced to die, his execution was indefinitely delayed by an influential noble in the capital. Guard Berton suspects political corruption or hidden foul play designed to spare or exploit the orc warlord.",al={"why is targorr alive","noble stay of execution"}},{q="Who gives the quest What Comes Around...?",a="Guard Berton gives the quest. He is stationed in Lakeshire within the Redridge Mountains, guarding the town against ongoing Blackrock orc incursions.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest"}},{q="Where can Targorr the Dread be found?",a="Targorr is held inside the Stormwind Stockade, situated in the canal district of Stormwind City. He can typically be found locked within a cell in the prison's central cell block.",al={"targorr location","where is targorr"}},{q="Who is General Gath'Ilzogg?",a="General Gath'Ilzogg is the warlord commanding the Blackrock orc forces occupying Stonewatch Keep in eastern Redridge Mountains, under whom Targorr served as executioner.",al={"gath'ilzogg","blackrock general redridge"}},{q="Why does Guard Berton take matters into his own hands?",a="Berton watched Redridge soldiers suffer and die under Targorr's blades. Disgusted that politicians in Stormwind are treating a ruthless murderer as a political pawn, he bypasses official bureaucracy to ensure true justice is served.",al={"berton motive","why bypass nobles"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The quest exposes the growing divide between frontline frontier garrisons like Lakeshire and the self-serving political machinations within Stormwind's noble courts.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the kingdom, executing Targorr settles personal debts for the atrocities committed against local town guards and militia during the Blackrock invasion of Redridge.",["class:Paladin"]="Bypassing corrupt legal stays to deliver retribution to an unrepentant torturer challenges the balance between codified law and genuine moral justice."},kw={"berton","blackrock","executioner","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","redridge","stockade","targorr"},rel={"npc:targorr-the-dread","npc:guard-berton","zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Guard Berton",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=386},src={"What Comes Around..."}}
E["quest:387"] = {t="quest",n="Quell The Uprising",z="stockade",s="Deep beneath the cobblestones of Stormwind, the high-security Stockade has fallen into total chaos. Following a coordinated breakout led by incarcerated members of the Defias Brotherhood, Warden Thelwater is urgently commissioning adventurers to cut down the rioting inmates and restore order before the capital learns how compromised the facility truly is.",h="Deep beneath the cobblestones of Stormwind, the high-security Stockade has fallen into total chaos.",sec={{t="A Prison Lost to Its Inmates",b="The Stockade was built to contain the most dangerous criminals, conspirators, and outlaws threatening the Kingdom of Stormwind. However, a sudden, violent uprising orchestrated by imprisoned Defias operatives has wrested control of the cell blocks directly from the guards. With the prison thoroughly overrun and corridors choked with armed felons, normal protocol has collapsed entirely. Rather than mounting a structured retaking, prison authorities are relying on visiting champions to fight their way through the riots.",sp=0},{t="Desperation and Cover-Up",b="Warden Thelwater's command to execute Defias prisoners on sight reflects both sheer desperation and an effort of self-preservation. Suspecting foul play behind the coordinated mutiny, the warden fears that if the broader nobility or the House of Nobles discovers the facility is out of hand, his post will be forfeit. By decreeing death as the immediate penalty for insurgency, Thelwater hopes brute force will break the inmates' spirits and quell the rebellion before word leaks past the canal gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Warden Thelwater asking adventurers to put down the riot?",a="The Stockade guards have lost control of the interior cells to the rioting Defias inmates. Warden Thelwater fears losing his position if the full scale of the disaster reaches the ears of Stormwind's leadership, so he recruits capable mercenaries to eliminate the ringleaders and re-establish control swiftly.",al={"why hire adventurers","thelwater motivation","why the stockade quest"}},{q="Who are the inmates rioting in the Stockade?",a="The core of the uprising consists of captured Defias Brotherhood members—including common prisoners, hardened convicts, and coordinated insurgents—who were locked away as the brotherhood waged its clandestine war across Westfall and Elwynn Forest.",al={"who is rioting","defias prisoners stockade","who broke out"}},{q="Does Thelwater believe the riot was an inside job?",a="Yes. Warden Thelwater openly suspects foul play, believing that a revolt this sudden and absolute could not have occurred purely by chance without outside interference or compromised security within the city.",al={"was it treason","foul play stockade","inside job prison"}},{q="Where does this uprising take place?",a="The uprising is contained—barely—inside The Stockade, a subterranean maximum-security dungeon located along the canals in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City.",al={"where is the stockade","stockade entrance","prison location"}},{q="What happens after these Defias rioters are killed?",a="While clearing out the insurgents dents the mutineers' ranks, Warden Thelwater admits upon your return that the crisis runs much deeper than a simple scuffle, requiring further strikes against high-profile leaders deeper within the cells.",al={"does the prison get safe","after quell the uprising"}},{q="Is lethal force authorized against all escaped convicts?",a="Warden Thelwater declares that the legal penalty for active insurgency during the takeover is immediate death, ordering champions to execute prisoners, convicts, and insurgents on the spot to force the surviving inmates into submission.",al={"why kill them","punishment for insurgency","is killing prisoners legal"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The rebellion inside the Stockade sits directly beneath Stormwind's streets, representing a catastrophic security lapse at the very heart of the Alliance's primary kingdom.",["race:Human"]="Many of the Defias inmates fighting in the cells are former kingdom stonemasons and common folk driven to rebellion, making the bloody riot a painful civil conflict for the people of Stormwind.",["class:Paladin"]="Restoring order in the bowels of the city tests the line between righteous justice and desperate, lethal retribution against rebellious citizens."},kw={"convicts","defias","insurgents","quell the uprising","stockade","stormwind","uprising","warden thelwater"},rel={"zone:stockade","npc:warden-thelwater","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Warden Thelwater",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=387},src={"Quell The Uprising"}}
E["quest:388"] = {t="quest",n="The Color of Blood",z="stockade",s="The Color of Blood is a personal task given by Nikova Raskol, a grieving grandmother living in Stormwind City. Consumed by anger over the murder of her young grandson inside the city's prison, she hires adventurers to venture into The Stockade and claim the Defias gang's trademark red bandanas as retribution.",h="The Color of Blood is a personal task given by Nikova Raskol, a grieving grandmother living in Stormwind City.",sec={{t="A Boy on the Prison Wall",b="When Stormwind's regular military forces were deployed away to distant fronts, local defense fell upon volunteer recruits and the city's youth. Nikova Raskol's grandson, Mac, was only fourteen years old when he took up arms as a guard within The Stockade. Tasked with watching hardened criminals and mutinous members of the Defias Brotherhood, the young guard was thrust into an intensely dangerous environment far beyond his experience.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Defiance",b="Behind bars, the captured Defias inmates began ripping apart their provided wool prison blankets, fashioning the shredded fabric into makeshift red bandanas. These crude garments served as identifying gang colors, signaling their continued loyalty to the Brotherhood even inside prison walls. When young Mac reprimanded the prisoners and tried to enforce discipline, the inmates stabbed the boy in the back, leaving him dead on the stone floor.",sp=0},{t="Grief and Vengeance",b="Devastated by Mac's pointless death, Nikova seeks cold revenge rather than official bureaucracy. She dispatches brave adventurers into the depths of The Stockade to cull the rioting prisoners and bring back ten of their cherished red bandanas—symbols dyed the color of her grandson's spilled blood. Presenting these blood-colored trophies offers a grim sense of closure to a broken family.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nikova Raskol?",a="Nikova Raskol is an elderly resident of Stormwind City whose fourteen-year-old grandson, Mac, was recently killed while serving as a guard inside The Stockade.",al={"nikova raskol","quest giver","who gives color of blood"}},{q="Why was a fourteen-year-old guarding dangerous prisoners?",a="With much of Stormwind's formal military sent away to the front lines, the city had to rely on inexperienced locals and youngsters to fill defensive positions, including guarding inmates in The Stockade.",al={"why was mac a guard","mac age","child guard"}},{q="Why do the Defias prisoners wear red wool bandanas?",a="The red bandanas are the unifying symbol of the Defias Brotherhood. While locked in The Stockade, inmates tore apart their woolen prison blankets to craft the red scarves and maintain their criminal solidarity.",al={"why red bandanas","wool bandanas lore","defias red scarves"}},{q="How did Mac Raskol die?",a="Mac caught prisoners shredding their wool blankets to make Defias gang scarves and reprimanded them. In response to his reprimand, the inmates stabbed the fourteen-year-old guard in the back.",al={"how did mac die","who killed mac","what happened to mac"}},{q="What does Nikova do with the bandanas?",a="She keeps them as proof of retribution. Staring at the torn wool tokens, she grieves the senseless loss of her grandson's life while finding peace knowing those who slew him faced justice.",al={"what happens to the bandanas","nikova bandanas"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The task sends you into The Stockade, Stormwind City's high-security prison located in the canal district, where the Defias prisoners are in open revolt.",al={"where do i get the bandanas","color of blood location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The death of Mac Raskol reveals the strain on Stormwind's home defense, showing the dire cost of deploying seasoned soldiers far from the capital.",["race:Human"]="Human citizens of Stormwind bear the brunt of Defias violence both in surrounding rural farmlands and right within the city walls."},kw={"color of blood","defias brotherhood","mac raskol","nikova raskol","red wool bandana","stockade","stormwind"},rel={"zone:stockade","npc:nikova-raskol","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Nikova Raskol",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=388},src={"The Color of Blood"}}
E["quest:391"] = {t="quest",n="The Stockade Riots",z="stockade",s="The Stockade Riots is an Alliance quest issued by Warden Thelwater at the gates of Stormwind's prison. To quell the ongoing uprising and prove your loyalty to the city guards, you are ordered to descend into the chaos and execute the riot's ringleader, Bazil Thredd.",h="The Stockade Riots is an Alliance quest issued by Warden Thelwater at the gates of Stormwind's prison.",sec={{t="Blood on the Stone",b="Deep beneath the cobblestones of the Mage Quarter, the Stockade has descended into utter lawlessness. Criminals, Defias insurgents, and violent cutthroats have broken containment and seized the cell blocks, turning the facility into an impenetrable war zone. Warden Thelwater and his guards are clinging desperately to the entrance, entirely unable to push inward and restore order through ordinary means.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Trust",b="Suspicious of anyone inquiring after Bazil Thredd, Warden Thelwater offers a brutal test of allegiances. Rather than granting a simple audience, he commands you to fight through the raging cell blocks, slay Thredd in his cell, and return carrying the rebel leader's severed head. Only by cutting down the figurehead of the uprising can an outsider prove they are not secretly aligned with the rebellion.",sp=1},{t="A Severed Thread",b="Killing Bazil Thredd delivers a decisive blow to the organization of the riot, though it also silences any direct answers he might have given regarding the conspiracy gripping Stormwind. Upon seeing Thredd's head, a surprised Thelwater concedes that the prisoner's death may make the prison manageable again, offering his own clues regarding Thredd's clandestine contacts before the insurrection erupted.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The Stockade Riots?",a="The quest is given by Warden Thelwater, who stands just inside the entrance tunnel of the Stockade in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"who gives the stockade riots","stockade riots quest giver","where to start stockade riots"}},{q="What do I need to do to complete the quest?",a="You must venture into the prison dungeon, locate the ringleader Bazil Thredd in the eastern cell block, execute him, and return his severed head to Warden Thelwater.",al={"stockade riots objective","how to beat stockade riots"}},{q="Where is Bazil Thredd located inside the Stockade?",a="From the entrance, follow the northern corridor up to the T-intersection, then proceed down the eastern cell block. Bazil Thredd is found in the center cell of a three-room chamber guarded by the ogre Hamhock.",al={"where is thredd","bazil thredd location","how to find thredd"}},{q="Why does Warden Thelwater want Bazil Thredd dead?",a="Bazil Thredd is the primary ringleader orchestrating the uprising within the facility. Thelwater believes cutting off the head of the revolt is the only way the guards can regain control of the rioting cell blocks, while also ensuring you are not secretly working for the rebels.",al={"why kill thredd","why thelwater wants thredd dead"}},{q="What happens after completing The Stockade Riots?",a="After turning in Thredd's head, Warden Thelwater directs you into the next stage of the investigation, sending you to investigate a mysterious figure who visited the prison prior to the riot in the quest The Curious Visitor.",al={"stockade riots follow up","what comes after stockade riots"},sp=1},{q="Can Horde players obtain this quest?",a="No. The Stockade Riots is strictly an Alliance quest, as the dungeon sits deep inside the capital city of Stormwind.",al={"is stockade riots alliance only","horde stockade riots"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="A full-scale revolt right beneath the Mage Quarter threatens the stability of Stormwind while the King remains missing and the kingdom is stretched thin.",["race:Human"]="Many of the rioters are Defias operatives and disgruntled stonemasons who turned on their own kingdom after the reconstruction dispute.",["class:Rogue"]="Infiltrating the riot offers a grim look at what happens when the Defias Brotherhood's clandestine underground network loses all restraint."},kw={"bazil thredd","defias","hamhock","stockade riots","stormwind","the stockade","warden thelwater"},rel={"quest:389","zone:stockade","npc:warden-thelwater","npc:hamhock","quest:392"},m={start="Warden Thelwater",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=391},src={"The Stockade Riots"}}
E["zone:stockade"] = {t="dungeon",n="The Stockade",z="stockade",s="The Stockade is Stormwind's high-security prison complex, tucked beneath the city's canal district near the Mage Quarter. Built to hold the kingdom's most dangerous cutthroats, political insurgents, and captured enemies of state, the facility has recently collapsed into violent anarchy. Warden Thelwater has been forced back to the threshold, desperately recruiting capable adventurers to crush the riot from within before it spills out into the capital.",h="The Stockade is Stormwind's high-security prison complex, tucked beneath the city's canal district near the...",sec={{t="A Prison Under Siege",b="Beneath the tranquil canals of Stormwind, the Stockade has become a war zone. When the regular army marched out to fight on distant fronts, the understaffed prison leaned on inexperienced youth—including fourteen-year-old recruits—to maintain order. It did not hold. The inmates launched a bloody, coordinated rebellion, tearing their wool blankets into gang scarves and cutting down the remaining guards. Warden Thelwater barely maintained control of the entryway, leaving the cells, hallways, and holding blocks in the ruthless hands of the convicts.",sp=0},{t="Nobles and Assassins",b="The riot laid bare the ugly underbelly of Stormwind's political machine. Outside territories had long grown frustrated with the House of Nobles halting executions for their own leverage. Redridge guard Berton wanted the captured orc Targorr the Dread executed for atrocities, only to watch nobles freeze the sentence. Darkshire councilman Millstipe watched the grave-robber Dextren Ward get spared the gallows despite desecrating graves for the necromancer Morbent Fel. Even the dwarves of Dun Modr sent word demanding the death of Dark Iron saboteur Kam Deepfury. With the Stockade in chaos, local authorities quietly hired adventurers to carry out the executions the capital's courts refused to enforce.",sp=1},{t="The Mastermind and the Enforcer",b="Behind the prison's synchronized collapse sits Bazil Thredd, a cunning felon tied directly to the Defias Brotherhood who orchestrated the uprising from his cell. Deep in the eastern cellblock lurks Bruegal Ironknuckle, a brutal dwarven brawler serving as the muscle of the revolt. While Thredd orchestrates the political disruption, Ironknuckle and his cohorts enforce absolute brutality within the halls. Striking down both the mastermind and his heavy enforcers is the only way Warden Thelwater can hope to break the inmates' spirits and reclaim the complex for the crown.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Stockade in open rebellion?",a="The Defias Brotherhood orchestrated a prison-wide riot while the facility was severely understaffed. With the Stormwind Army deployed to distant battlefronts, teenage volunteers were left guarding hardened killers. The convicts ambushed the staff, seized weapons, and forced Warden Thelwater out of the cellblocks.",al={"why riot","what happened in stockades","stockades riot cause"}},{q="Who is running the uprising inside?",a="The mastermind behind the revolt is Bazil Thredd, an influential Defias felon incarcerated in the central corridor. He coordinated the prisoners across factions, using enforcers like the dwarven rogue Bruegal Ironknuckle, the ogre Hamhock, and Dark Iron infiltrator Kam Deepfury to hold the wings.",al={"stockades boss","who leads the riot","who runs stockades"}},{q="Why are prisoners like Targorr and Dextren Ward still alive?",a="Both were condemned to death, but corrupt politicians within the House of Nobles placed bureaucratic holds on their executions to use them as political leverage. This interference outraged allies in Lakeshire and Darkshire, prompting them to send adventurers to eliminate the prisoners during the chaos.",al={"why wasn't targorr executed","dextren ward court","house of nobles corruption"}},{q="What does defeating Bruegal Ironknuckle mean for the prison?",a="Bruegal Ironknuckle is the most fearsome enforcer among the rioters. Striking down this rare dwarven brawler shatters the physical intimidation holding the inmates together, leaving Bazil Thredd without his primary muscle and allowing Warden Thelwater to begin restoring order.",al={"bruegal ironknuckle lore","kill bruegal","who is bruegal"}},{q="Why are there Dark Iron dwarves and orcs inside a human jail?",a="The Stockade serves as a maximum-security holding pen for high-value prisoners of war. Targorr the Dread led Blackrock orc attacks in Redridge, while Kam Deepfury conducted sabotage for the Dark Iron clan in the Wetlands before both were captured and transferred to the capital.",al={"why dark irons here","kam deepfury lore","targorr stockades"}},{q="Can Horde players enter the Stockade?",a="Yes, but it is exceptionally hazardous. The dungeon entrance sits directly inside Stormwind City near the Mage Quarter canals. Horde infiltrators must sneak past city guards and Alliance players through the harbor and sewer system to reach the portal.",al={"can horde do stockades","horde in stormwind prison"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The rebellion threatens the very heart of the capital; putting down the uprising preserves Stormwind's internal security while honoring off-the-books bounties for Redridge, Duskwood, and Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="The presence of Kam Deepfury in Stormwind's cells is an affront to Dun Modr; the Kingdom of Ironforge demands his head to avenge dwarven lives lost in the Wetlands.",["class:Rogue"]="The prison layout presents an intricate web of locked iron cells and Defias connections, offering unique lockpicking practice and insight into Bazil Thredd's underworld syndicate.",["class:Mage"]="Located right on the canal edge of the Mage Quarter, the riot's physical brawlers and lack of hostile spellcasters make defensive wards and Amplify Magic especially effective for support."},kw={"bazil thredd","bruegal ironknuckle","canals","defias","dextren ward","hamhock","kam deepfury","riot","stockade","stormwind","targorr","warden thelwater"},rel={"npc:warden-thelwater","npc:bruegal-ironknuckle","npc:kam-deepfury","npc:targorr-the-dread","npc:dextren-ward","quest:391","quest:389"},m={levels="24-32"},src={"Stormwind Stockade (Classic)","Stormwind Stockade"}}
